// ROUGE-V canonical kernels: every supported mma.sync form (Wave 3 step 2).
//
// Per form two entries share the fragment counts (nA/nB/nD) but differ
// in values:
//   <form>_ones: every A/B element is exactly 1.0 (or 1), C is 0, so every
//     D element is exactly K (16 or 8) — hand-verifiable bit patterns that
//     prove decode, accumulation and encode for the form.
//   <form>_lane: A = BASE|lane, B = BASE|(lane+100), C = 0 — every lane
//     publishes distinct fragments, so any peer mix-up in the exchange
//     changes D. The reference is the interpreter itself (AOT test).
// 1.0 payloads: f16 0x3C00, bf16 0x3F80, e4m3 0x38, e5m2 0x3C, u8/s8 0x01.
.version 9.4
.target sm_75
.address_size 64

